<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine monthly grain/oilseed shipments.</title>
<headline>Argentine monthly grain/oilseed shipments.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agriculture Secretariat September grain shipment figures (tonnes), followed by January-September totals (year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> Wheat	249,998   (92,515)     3,289,609  (6,010,163)</p>
<p> Maize	315,882  (337,605)     6,252,185  (5,569,924)</p>
<p> Sorghum     13,941   (20,663)	 648,555    (168,525)</p>
<p> Barley	   nil	(nil)	   6,888     (21,401)</p>
<p> Soybeans   106,848    (1,467)     2,075,998  (2,580,846)</p>
<p> Sunseed	  527   (14,901)	 536,974    (824,389)</p>
<p> Others	11,152   (21,711)	 212,432    (200,085)</p>
<p>Principal destinations in September were as follows (tonnes):</p>
<p>WHEAT: Brazil 216,608; Kenya 22,891; Chile 7,701</p>
<p>MAIZE: Peru 4,747; Lebanon 34,095; Algeria 29,501; Cuba 26,073; Kuwait 231; United Kingdom 64,682</p>
<p>-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0668</p>
